      "worked": "In one-variable statistics, enter $12,14,16,18$ in $x$ and $13,6,2,12$ in Freq. The median result is $\\operatorname{med}=14$.\n\nCheck the middle position:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=13+6+2+12\\\\n&=33\\\\M_p&=\\frac{33+1}{2}\\\\M_p&=17\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe cumulative frequencies are $13,19,21,33$. The 17th observation lies among the scores of $14$, so the median is $14$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
